# Proof of the Linnik 1951 entry

`LeanLab/Linnik1951/Burst1122RouteFinal.lean` proves `linnik1951_decomposed_final_b1122`:
assuming the generalized Riemann hypothesis for Dirichlet L-functions, some `K` makes every
sufficiently large even integer a sum of two primes and at most `K` powers of two. This is the
qualitative form of the theorem of Yu. V. Linnik, Prime numbers and powers of two, Trudy Mat.
Inst. Steklov 38, 1951, page 154. The files it imports are listed in `PORTING.md`. Binary
Goldbach is open and is not claimed. AI agents wrote the Lean code, see `PORTING.md`; it was
checked by the Lean kernel.
